===========================================================================
EXERCISE 5.1: DC OFFSET ARTIFACT ON AUTOCORRELATION
===========================================================================
Signal s[n]: [-1000, -1000, 1000, 1000, -1000, -1000, 1000, 1000] (mean = 0.0)
DC offset c = 500.0, x[n] = [-500, -500, 1500, 1500, -500, -500, 1500, 1500] (mean = 500.0)
tau |    Rs[tau] |    Rx[tau] |  Rw[tau] |      rs[tau] |      rx[tau] |    rx - rs
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  0 |  8000000.0 | 10000000.0 |      8.0 |   1000000.00 |   1250000.00 |  250000.00
  1 |  1000000.0 |  2750000.0 |      7.0 |    142857.14 |    392857.14 |  250000.00
  2 | -6000000.0 | -4500000.0 |      6.0 |  -1000000.00 |   -750000.00 |  250000.00
  3 | -1000000.0 |   250000.0 |      5.0 |   -200000.00 |     50000.00 |  250000.00
  4 |  4000000.0 |  5000000.0 |      4.0 |   1000000.00 |   1250000.00 |  250000.00

Decomposition Analysis:
  Rx[tau] = Rs[tau] + c * [sum_{n=0}^{N-1-tau} s[n] + sum_{n=tau}^{N-1} s[n]] + c^2 * Rw[tau]
  When the partial window sums of s[n] vanish, rx[tau] - rs[tau] = c^2 = 250000.0.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

