EXERCISE 5.2: RECIPROCAL MULTIPLIER DERIVATION FOR L = 426, 640, 800
===========================================================================
Span L = 426:
  Max biased sum: 27918123 (requires 25 bits)
  Minimal shift k: 26
  Optimal multiplier M = ceil(2^26 / 426) = 157533 (Hex: 0x2675D, 18 bits)
  Product width: 43 bits
Span L = 640:
  Max biased sum: 41942720 (requires 26 bits)
  Minimal shift k: 25
  Optimal multiplier M = ceil(2^25 / 640) = 52429 (Hex: 0xCCCD, 16 bits)
  Product width: 42 bits
Span L = 800:
  Max biased sum: 52428400 (requires 26 bits)
  Minimal shift k: 27
  Optimal multiplier M = ceil(2^27 / 800) = 167773 (Hex: 0x28F5D, 18 bits)
  Product width: 44 bits
