===========================================================================
EXERCISE 5.3: INTEL CYCLONE V DSP BLOCK MAPPING FOR 25x24 MULTIPLIER
===========================================================================
Cyclone V Variable-Precision DSP Block Capabilities (CV-52003):
  1. Independent Multiplier Modes per Variable-Precision DSP Block:
     - Three 9x9 multipliers
     - Two 18x18 (or 18x19) multipliers
     - One 27x27 multiplier (either signed or unsigned)
  2. Local Mean Multiplier Dimensions:
     - Operand A: S_biased, 25 bits unsigned (0 to 27,918,123)
     - Operand B: M = 10,082,083, 24 bits unsigned
     - Since 25 <= 27 and 24 <= 27:
       A 25x24 unsigned multiplication fits ENTIRELY inside ONE Cyclone V DSP block in 27x27 mode!
     - Resource consumption: EXACTLY 1 DSP Block, 0 ALM logic for multiplication.
  3. Comparison if synthesized in soft ALM logic:
     - 25x24 unsigned multiplier in soft logic requires ~300 to 450 ALMs.
     - Dedicated DSP hardware saves routing congestion and guarantees timing closure at 50 MHz.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

===========================================================================
EXERCISE 5.4: DC-BLOCKER CUTOFF FREQUENCIES AND WORDLENGTH
===========================================================================
 Shift r |   alpha = 1 - 2^-r |   Exact fc (-3dB) (Hz) |    Approx (1-a)*fs/2pi |   Gain @ 75Hz (dB)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
       7 |         0.99218750 |                19.8172 |                19.8944 |            -0.2635
       8 |         0.99609375 |                 9.9278 |                 9.9472 |            -0.0590
       9 |         0.99804688 |                 4.9687 |                 4.9736 |            -0.0106

Internal State Wordlength Requirement:
  Difference equation: y[n] = x[n] - x[n-1] + alpha * y[n-1] = dx[n] + y[n-1] - (y[n-1] >> r)
  If y[n] is stored in 16 bits with no fractional bits, the shift (y[n-1] >> 8) truncates to 0
  whenever |y[n-1]| < 256, creating a DC limit cycle of amplitude up to +/-255!
  By extending the internal accumulator to Q16.16 (32 bits total, 16 integer + 16 fractional):
  The feedback resolution is 2^-16 = 0.000015, eliminating limit cycles and quantization DC drift.
===========================================================================
